{
  "requirement": "The `PlainText` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct PlainText;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for PlainText;\nimpl Debug for PlainText;\nimpl Default for PlainText;\nimpl OutlineLang for PlainText;\nimpl Copy for PlainText;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText` has two parts. It declares the unit struct `PlainText` with trait impls for Clone, Debug, Default, OutlineLang and Copy. It also says `PlainText` supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter.\n\n- **Declaration and trait impls:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc. Through `check_declaration` it asserts that the declared trait implementations match rustdoc's `trait_impls` for each documented item. It also asserts that indexed members match. This checks the struct and its listed impls against the book text. I did not read the helper bodies beyond the search excerpts.\n- **Extension rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` constructs `languages::PlainText` and asserts `name()` is \"plain-text\" and `extensions()` is empty. Both are `OutlineLang` methods.\n- **Selection rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors]` covers the root item and the \"line\" items for nonblank lines. It checks `line@<12 hex>` selectors, equal selectors for duplicate lines, selecting by selector, and the empty input. It also checks that unclaimed filenames such as \"missing.unclaimed\" and \"README\" fall back to plain text.\n- **Fingerprint rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries]` checks the SHA-256 value, whitespace normalisation, word boundaries and the scheme string. The first test above also checks whole-content structural and fingerprint behavior.\n\nThe detailed rules belong to the sibling requirements `plain-text.items` and `plain-text.fingerprints`. This requirement only needs the type to exist with those impls and to supply those rules, and the tests above cover that. I found no gaps.",
